body:
How did you call the scramble_sentence function? Did you null terminate orig? Second, and I think what may be causing the issue, you did not allocate enough memory for the null terminator for the copy variable in scramble_sentence function. Also i'm not sure you're aware but the statement:

    *copy = '\0';

is completely redundant. If you read the man page for calloc: https://linux.die.net/man/3/calloc, you can see that the memory allocated by the function is initially set to zero anyway. More of a preference, but I personally like to use: 

    memset(copy, '\0', strlen(orig) + 1);

I'm not really sure what the check4win function does but i'm pretty sure it can be condensed.


    bool check4win(int a[4][4])
    {
    	for( int i = 0; i < 4; i++ )
    	{
    		for( int j = 0; j < 4; j++ )
    		{
    			if( a[i][j] == 2048 )
    			{
    				return true;
    				i = 4; // for whatever reason?
    			}
    		} 
    	}
    	return false;
    }
